@startuml backup-manager
title What the manager asks of the host: a new configuration, an archive to read off-site, the archives found off-site

skinparam dpi 110
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ConditionStyle diamond
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #555555
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4D6
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #B8860B
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #999999
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold

|#FAFAFA|1. Manager, root only\nBackups|
start
if (Root account?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:403: the Backups page and
  everything under it are root only
  No permission opens them;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Backup installed on the server?\n(configuration published)) then (no)
  :Nothing to configure:
  the manager never installs
  nor removes the backup;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:**Backups > Configure**
Time, backups kept,
off-site destination user@host:/path,
box "delete here once sent";
note right
  No script, no command:
  four values, nothing else
  The off-site destination is only
  set here, never at install
  The archives folder is read only
end note

|#FFF3E0|2. manager-api|
if (Values valid?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:400, nothing written;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
#FFE2B8:Write **request.conf** in the folder
shared with the host
Record the change in the activity journal;
:Answer "pending";

|#F1F8F1|3. Host\nbackup.apply.sh, every minute|
if (request.conf there?) then (no)
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Every value valid\n**again**, backup installed?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Change nothing
  status.conf = error + reason;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
#D9F2D9:Rewrite **backup.conf**
(the archives folder is kept);
#D9F2D9:Rewrite the **cron entry**
with the new time;
#D9F2D9:Publish the configuration again
status.conf = applied;

|#FAFAFA|4. Manager|
:The page shows "applied"
or the reason of the refusal;
stop

|#FAFAFA|1. Manager, root only\nBackups|
start
:**Backups**, list of the archives
Download an archive that was
sent off-site and deleted here;
note right
  The manager cannot reach the
  other server: only root on the
  host holds the ssh key
  The archive goes from the other
  server to the browser: it is never
  written on this server
end note

|#FFF3E0|2. manager-api|
if (Archive still kept off-site,\nat the place the database holds?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:404, nothing asked;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Another archive being downloaded\nfrom off-site?) then (yes)
  #FFD9D9:409, nothing asked;
  stop
else (no)
endif
#FFE2B8:Write **retrieve.conf**: the name,
the place
Record it in the activity journal;

|#F1F8F1|3. Host\nbackup.apply.sh, every minute|
if (Name of an archive, place\nuser@host:/path, archive found\nthere **over ssh**?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Read nothing
  retrieve-status.conf = error + reason;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
#D9F2D9:Make the pipe **retrieve.pipe**
retrieve-status.conf = ready,
with the size found there;

|#FAFAFA|4. Manager|
:The download starts by itself:
the browser is handed the pipe;

|#F1F8F1|3. Host\nbackup.apply.sh, every minute|
if (A browser came to read\nwithin two minutes?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Nothing was read off-site
  Remove the pipe
  retrieve-status.conf = error + reason;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
#D9F2D9:Feed the pipe from the other server
**over ssh**, as the browser reads
Nothing is written on this server;
if (Read to the end?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:Remove the pipe
  retrieve-status.conf = error + reason;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
#D9F2D9:Remove the pipe
retrieve-status.conf = done;
stop

|#FAFAFA|1. Manager, root only\nBackups|
start
:**Backups**, list of the archives
Show where each archive is;

|#FFF3E0|2. manager-api|
if (An archive kept off-site, at the\ndestination of backup.conf?) then (no)
  :Nothing to check off-site;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
if (Last listing less than a minute old\n**and** made after the last archive was sent?) then (yes)
  :Show what that listing found;
  stop
else (no)
endif
#FFE2B8:Write **offsite-request.conf**
It names no place
An archive sent after the last listing
is shown as being checked,
never as not there;

|#F1F8F1|3. Host\nbackup.apply.sh, every minute|
:List the off-site destination
of **backup.conf** **over ssh**,
never a place the manager gives;
if (Reached?) then (no)
  #FFD9D9:offsite.conf = error;
else (yes)
  #D9F2D9:offsite.conf = the archives
  found there, and when;
endif

|#FAFAFA|4. Manager|
:The page loads again by itself
Each archive sent off-site is shown
present or not there, as found there
Only "sent" when it could not be checked;
stop
@enduml
